  ],
  "mach:judgement": "Caution",
  "mach:judgementReason": "Strong nucleus segmentation model — Medical Image Analysis 2024, state-of-the-art on PanNuke, ViT-based WSI inference. However, licensed under Apache 2.0 with Commons Clause, which prohibits selling the software and is not OSI-approved open source. This non-standard licence creates legal ambiguity for commercial and many institutional use cases. Consider HoVer-Net (MIT) or StarDist (BSD-3-Clause) as alternatives with clean open-source licences. CellViT++ is the actively maintained successor.",
